ess","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Who can be designee:** Under Rule 2a-5, the board may designate the fund's **primary investment adviser**. This excludes any sub-adviser. The board may also perform fair value determinations itself. For funds without a board, such as UITs, the trustee or depositor may serve. The designee may use sub-advisers and pricing services but stays responsible and must oversee them.\n\n**Required reporting to the board:**\n- **Quarterly:** written reports with information the board reasonably requests and a summary or description of material changes in fair value methodologies, pricing services, or valuation risks.\n- **At least annually:** a written assessment of the adequacy and effectiveness of the fair value process. This covers valuation risk assessment, methodologies, testing, and pricing service oversight.\n- **Prompt reporting:** material matters, such as material weaknesses or errors in fair value determinations, within the time the board sets. This is no later than **five business days** after the designee becomes aware.\n\nThe designee must also specify personnel and segregate functions. The fund must keep records supporting determinations and reports.","ttft_ms":3863,"type":"result","duration_ms":7459,"uuid":"35b48e11-055c-4145-93ba-95a92b22149f","ttft_stream_ms":552,"time_to_request_ms":71,"first_content_frame_ms":552,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
